All 7 remaining possibilities are "needs two" machines. The machine is not "needs one", because a "needs one" pair would have made the last test light up.

The 7 possible nexiom pairs are:
- {doveda, salozer}
- {lutufur, salozer}
- {detamo, salozer}
- {detamo, milaren}
- {detamo, letanun}
- {milaren, salozer}
- {letanun, salozer}

Two more tests can separate at most 4 cases, so I can't guarantee certainty. I'll split the cases as evenly as possible.

This test splits them 3 and 4:
- **Lights (3):** {doveda, salozer}, {lutufur, salozer}, or {detamo, salozer}.
- **Doesn't light (4):** {detamo, milaren}, {detamo, letanun}, {milaren, salozer}, or {letanun, salozer}.

TEST: doveda, lutufur, detamo, salozer

The machine needs two nexioms, and salozer is one of them. The last test lit up, so both nexioms were among doveda, lutufur, detamo and salozer. That leaves 3 possible pairs:
- {doveda, salozer}
- {lutufur, salozer}
- {detamo, salozer}

One test can only split these into 1 and 2, so I can't guarantee certainty.

Testing doveda and salozer together:
- **Lights:** the nexioms are doveda and salozer.
- **Doesn't light:** it's lutufur or detamo with salozer, and I'll have to guess between them.

TEST: doveda, salozer
